      "writtenOn": "2021-06-15T09:47:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m concerned that this method is making a decision based on state (mActiveTetheringRequests) that is forgotten soon after this method runs. I think that could potentially cause incorrect behaviour when stopping tethering.\n\nWhat is the intent of this method? Is it so that a given device can support using NCM for USB tethering (e.g., enabled by startTethering(TETHERING_USB) but also support using NCM tethering enabled by startTethering(TETHERING_NCM)?\n\nIf so, is that something that we need to support?\n\nCould we simply say that if a device has set config_tether_usb_functions to 1 (i.e., set USB tethering to use NCM by default) then calling startTethering(TETHERING_NCM) is exactly the same as calling startTethering(TETHERING_USB)?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 855,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 859,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "d3db192e941813478f84f57d15a2c1217366e8a2",
